SOAPBOX: Trying a Multi-Single with internet remote operators.  Actually
SOAPBOX: for this contest, working in a VNC windows is not much different
SOAPBOX: than working from home.   Really no difference. This was a part
SOAPBOX: time operation while I was traveling, which gave me the idea to
SOAPBOX: team up with long time friend  AC8Y and his fine station for this
SOAPBOX: effort.   My biggest complaint is working off a 15.7 inch laptop
SOAPBOX: screen.   The N1MM integeration with WSJT-X worked perfectly.
SOAPBOX: Many contacts sending a signal report and not in contest mode
SOAPBOX: with sequence issues.  I would try to get ahead of it and send a
SOAPBOX: forced RR73 and move on.  I need to look at last years score but
SOAPBOX: I feel like less operators in the contest running in contest
SOAPBOX: mode.  Never went to 10 or 160 meters.   15M was good but I was
SOAPBOX: not on for some of the prime 15M hours.  40M was good on Sunday
SOAPBOX: morning for picking up OC mults and contacts at 6 points each.
SOAPBOX: In setting up for the contest, I had some repeated walk throughs
SOAPBOX: of the great setup guide at RTTYcontesting.com.   I have gone
SOAPBOX: through this enough times I should be an expert.  Hi HI   see you
SOAPBOX: next time.
